              %path{:d => "M -2.487623 2.868735 C -2.03161 1.146892 -1.021305 0.333145 0.000793428 -0.00100268 C -1.021305 -0.33515 -2.03161 -1.148898 -2.487623 -2.87074 ", :style => "fill:none;stroke-width:0.47818;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round;stroke:rgb(0%,0%,0%);stroke-opacity:1;stroke-miterlimit:10;", :transform => "matrix(0.993667,0,0,-0.993667,84.04218,78.592754)"}
              %g{:style => "fill:rgb(0%,0%,0%);fill-opacity:1;"}
                %use{:x => "53.930265", "xlink:href" => "#AYypTjsxuzftgsBmE0BwUm66klk=-glyph1-5", :y => "86.348322"}
          %p
            there is a unique tight morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi T
                  %mi u
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \colon X \rightarrow T u
            such that
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi τ
                      %mi u
                    %mi x
                    %mo =
                    %mi ξ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tau_{u} x = \xi
          %ol
            %li
              The tetrahedron condition holds (see
              = succeed ")." do
                %a{:href => "#Pare2011"} Paré, page 478
          %p
            If only the first universal property holds, we say that the loose morphism has a
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
                \-tabulator
          %h2#properties Properties
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                A double category
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝔻
                      %mo =
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi D
                        %mn 0
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi D
                        %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{D} = (D_{0}, D_{1})
                has all
                = succeed "-tabulators" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
                = succeed "-cotabulators)" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
                = succeed "-assigning" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+morphisms"} identity
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi id
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %msub
                        %mi D
                        %mn 0
                      %mo →
                      %msub
                        %mi D
                        %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} id \colon D_{0} \rightarrow D_{1}
                has a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+adjoint"} right adjoint
                (resp.
                = succeed ")." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
            %li
              %p
                A double category has all small
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/double+limits"} double limits
                if and only if it has small double products, double equalisers, and tabulators.
            %li
              %p
                A tabulator in a
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-category"} 2-category
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/double+category"} double category
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/power"} power
                by the
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/interval+category"} interval category
          %h2#references References
          %p
            An early reference for what is essentially the universal property of an (effective) tabulator is the definition of a
            = succeed "," do
              %strong tabulation
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/allegory"} allegory
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Aurelio+Carboni"}> Aurelio Carboni
              ,
              %span.newWikiWord
                Stefano Kasangian
                %a{:href => "/nlab/new/Stefano+Kasangian"} ?
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ross+Street"} Ross Street
              = succeed "," do
                %em Bicategories of spans and relations
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0022-4049(84)90061-6"} doi:10.1016/0022-4049(84)90061-6
          %p The definition of a (co)tabulator was first introduced in Section 5.3 of:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Marco+Grandis"}> Marco Grandis
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Robert+Pare"} Robert Pare
              = succeed "," do
                %em Limits in double categories
              = succeed "," do
                %strong 40
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.numdam.org/item/CTGDC_1999__40_3_162_0/"} url
          %p
            The
            = succeed "-dimensional" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2
          %ul
            %li#Pare2011
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Robert+Pare"}> Robert Pare
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Yoneda theory for double categories
              = succeed "," do
                %strong 25
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.tac.mta.ca/tac/volumes/25/17/25-17abs.html"} url
          %p Other references on (co)tabulators include:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Susan+Niefield"}> Susan Niefield
                ,
                %em Span, cospan, and other double categories
                Theory and Applications of Categories_,
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 26
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.tac.mta.ca/tac/volumes/26/26/26-26abs.html"} url
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Marco+Grandis"} Marco Grandis
                and
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bob+Par%C3%A9"} Bob Paré
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Span and cospan representations of weak double categories
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.mscs.dal.ca/~pare/DblRpr.pdf"} url
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Marco+Grandis"}> Marco Grandis
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Higher Dimensional Categories. From Double to Multiple Categories
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1142/11406"} doi:10.1142/11406
